2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAVARRE.htm#AssonaIniguez
2 CONT
2 CONT Íñigo "Arista" & his wife ONECA had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GARCÍA Iñíguez ([810]-killed by Arabs [Lumberri] 882[57], bur Leire Monastery).  The Codex de Roda names "Garsea Enneconis et domna Assona…et domna ---" as the children of "Enneco cognomento Aresta"[58].  He succeeded h
2 CONC is father in [852] as GARCÍA I [King] of Pamplona.  He was defeated by the Muslims in [858].  "Rexo Garsia, filius Eneconis" donated property to the monastery of Leire, with the advice of "filii mei Fortunii", by charter dated 21 
2 CONC Oct 880[59].  This is the only source so far identified which accords the royal title to García and it is not clear whether it was contemporary.  The Libro de Regla of Leire Monastery, compiled in 1076, records that "filius eius G
2 CONC arsea Ennecones" ruled for 12 years after the death of "Enneco Xemenones" and died "era DCCCXXXV…in Lumberri", his body being returned "ad monasterium Legeren" (for burial)[60]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [firstly] URRACA, daughter of ---.  An undated charter refers to a confirmation by “rex domnus Garcia et regina domna Urraca maiore”[61].  Her origin is not known.  Rodrigo Ximénez de Rada, writing in the first half of the 13th 
2 CONC century, records that "Enecho…Arista…filium Garsiam" married "Urracam, de Regio semine"[62].  Jaurgain suggests that "de Regio semine" should be interpreted as meaning "de la même race que lui" (based on his assumption that the ki
2 CONC ngs of Navarre were descended from the dukes of Gascony, about which there appears to be no proof) and that Urraca was "fille de Sanche-Sancion duc de Vasconie", although he cites no primary source which confirms this parentage[63
2 CONC ].  Her origin is discussed by Salazar y Acha who suggests that she was a member of the Banu Qasi family, related to the second wife of Fruela II King of Asturias, which would account for the introduction of the name Fortún into t
2 CONC he family of the kings of Navarre[64].  
2 CONT
2 CONT [m secondly LEODEGUNDIS de Asturias, daughter of [ORDOÑO I King of Asturias & his wife Munia ---].  The manuscript of the Codex de Roda entitled "Versi domna Leodegundia regina" names "Leodegundiam Ordonii filiam" and indicates he
2 CONC r position as Queen of Pamplona after her marriage[65].  She is not named in the genealogies in the earlier part of the Codex de Roda.  She has been suggested as a possible second wife of King García I but, as there is no indicati
2 CONC on of dates in the "Versi", this is mere speculation.  Barrau-Dihigo casts doubt on this identification[66].  It is of course possible that she was not a historical figure at all.  It may have been convenient for chroniclers of th
2 CONC e rulers of Pamplona to invent a dynastic connection with the kings of Asturias in order to boost local credibility.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT García I & his [first] wife had [four] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         FORTÚN García ([830]-after 905).  The Codex de Roda names "Fortunio Garseanis et Sanzio Garseanis et domna Onneca" as the children of "Garsea Enneconis" and his unnamed wife[67].  He succeeded his father in 882 as FORT
2 CONC ÚN [King] of Pamplona. See below.
2 CONT * b)         SANCHO García .  The Codex de Roda names "Fortunio Garseanis et Sanzio Garseanis et domna Onneca" as the children of "Garsea Enneconis" and his unnamed wife[68].  m ---.  The name of Sancho's wife is not known.  Sanch
2 CONC o García & his wife had [two] children: …
2 CONT * c)         ONECA García.  The Codex de Roda names "Fortunio Garseanis et Sanzio Garseanis et domna Onneca" as the children of "Garsea Enneconis" and his unnamed wife, stating that Oneca married "Asnari Galindones de Aragone"[77]
2 CONC .  m AZNAR [II] Galíndez Conde de Aragón, son of GALINDO [I] Aznar Conde de Aragón & his wife --- (-893). 
2 CONT * d)         [JIMENA (-after Jun 912, bur [Astorga, transferred to Oviedo Santa María]).  m ([869/70]) ALFONSO III “el Magno” King of Asturias, son of ORDOÑO I King of Asturias & his wife Munia --- (848-20 Dec 910).] 
2 CONT * García & his [wife/mistress] had one [illegitimate] child: e)         daughter .  Ibn Hayyan´s Muqtabis II records "la hija de Garsiya ibn W.n.q." as the wife of "Amrus ibn Amr ibn Amrus" in A.H. 259 [872/73][85].  It is possibl
2 CONC e that this daughter of [King] García was illegitimate.  m as his (x) wife, AMRUS ibn Umar Wali [governor/king] of Huesca, son of UMAR ibn Amrus (-[Huesca] Apr 875). 
2 CONT
