2 CONT Statue in Madrid (José Oñate, 1750–53).
2 CONT
2 CONT Íñigo Íñiguez Arista (Arabic: ونّقه بن ونّقه‎, Wannaqo ibn Wannaqo, Basque: Eneko Enekones Aritza/Haritza/Aiza; c. 790 – 851 or 852) was the first King of Pamplona (c. 824 – 851 or 852). He is said by a later chronicler to have be
2 CONC en count of Bigorre, or at least to have come from there, but there is no near-contemporary evidence of this.[1]
2 CONT
