1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Pero Fromarigues de Guimarães==
2 CONT
2 CONT Pero Fromarigues de Guimarães (c.1080-?) was a Portuguese nobleman, Lord of Melo
2 CONT
2 CONT Pero was the son of Fromarigo Guterres,[2] great-grandson of Sueiro Belfaguer, and a descendant of the knights of Kingdom of León.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT GENEALOGY by Manuel da Silva Costa | mscosta2000@hotmail.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Pacheco is very old. At the behest of Julius Caesar, Vivio Pacheco defended Ulia (Basque Country), surrounded by the troops of Pompey (45 BC) ...
2 CONT
2 CONT The earliest direct ascendant known to the " Pacheco, " Fromarigo Guterres, was married to Elvira Gulfara, living in 1167. She received feuds in Guimarães and Esposende (1110). By D. Afonso Henriques was Alcaide de Guimarães and A
2 CONC lcaide (1131) and Butler (1139) of Coimbra ( http://www.soveral.info/mas/Ribadouro%20e%20Pacheco.htm )
2 CONT Pero Fromarigues was son of the previous ones and father of Fernão Peres.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernão Peres de Guimarães, a knight of Coimbra, documented between 1160 and 1178, married to Usco Godins (daughter of Godinho Fafes de Lanhoso and Ouroana "Gontinha" Mendes) was the father of Pedro Fernandes. Pedro Fernandes de Ca
2 CONC mbra married Maria Ourigues (daughter of Ourigo "o Velho" da Nobrega and Maria Lourenço da Cunha) and had, among others, Soeiro Pires Pacheco and Tereja Pires de Cambra. Tereja Pires de Cambra was married to Rui Pires de Ferreira 
2 CONC (son of Pero Pais and Tereja Ramires Carpinteiro), Rico-man of D. Afonso II. His children Maria, Urraca or Elvira and Fernão Rodrigues adopted the nickname Pacheco of the maternal uncle Soeiro Pires.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernão Rodrigues Pacheco went with his wife Constança Afonso (daughter of Afonso Anes de Cambra and Urraca Pires Ribeiro) 5 the Lords of Ferreira de Aves (Sátão). As Mayor of Celorico da Beira, by D. Sancho II with his brother use
2 CONC d the morning to serve a trout that an eagle dropped on the Castle, the besiegers to show that it had provisions (1246) ... The children John , Martim and Fernão were nicknamed Pacheco .  Already in 1524, in Loulé, in the Acts of 
2 CONC Vereação, is Martim Pacheco , about fines.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duarte Pacheco was born in Loulé in 1900. He graduated in electrotechnical engineering (1923) by IS Technician, of which he was assistant (1924), professor (1925) and director (1926). Minister of Public Instruction (1928) and Publ
2 CONC ic Works (1932), passed away (1943) on his way to the Council of Ministers to deal with the Lajes Agreement ...
2 CONT
