3 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Ermengol
1 NOTE Wifred (Catalan: Guifré, Spanish: Vifredo or Wifredo; c. 970 - 1050) was the Count of Cerdanya (988-1035; as Wifred II) and Count of Berga (1003-1035; as Wifred I). He was the eldest son of Oliba Cabreta and Ermengard of Ampurias
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT When his father abdicated in 988 to become a monk in Monte Cassino, Wifred's brother Bernard received Besalú while Oliba received Berga. Their mother acted as regent until 994. When Oliba followed his father into the church in 10
2 CONC 03, his county passed to Wifred. In that year Wifred and Bernard joined an alliance of Christian princes to fend off a Muslim invasion at the Battle of Torà.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Like his father and brother before him, he had a great affection for the church. He participated actively in the consecration of many churches and monasteries, such as San Martín del Canigó, founded in 1007 and consecrated in 10
2 CONC 09. Despite this, he did fight to free his county from the jurisdiction of the diocese of Urgell and thus entered into conflict with Saint Ermengol.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1023, Wifred entered into a peace concord with Berengar Raymond I of Barcelona and William I of Besalú. In the early thirteenth-century Liber feudorum Ceritaniae the first folio is illuminated with a scene of Wifred receiving 
2 CONC the homage of sarn and Dalmau, lords of Castellfollit. The picture, painted by a different artist from the rest of book, is of a higher calibre than the otherss and is in the Byzantinist style that was becoming dominant in Catalon
2 CONC ia around 1200.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1035, he finally followed his father and brother into monastic retirement, becoming a monk in his own foundation of San Martín del Canigó. He died some fifteen years later in 1050. By his marriage to Guisla of Pallars, he had
2 CONC  many children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Raymond (1035-1068), successor in Cerdanya 
2 CONT Wifred (d. 1079), archbishop of Narbonne 
2 CONT Berengar (d. 1053), bishop of Elna 
2 CONT Arduin (d. 1050) 
2 CONT William Wifred (d. 1075), bishop of Urgell 
2 CONT Bernard (d. 1050), successor in Berga 
2 CONT Berengar (d. 1093), successor of Bernard in Berga and bishop of Girona 
2 CONT Fe (also Fides or Foy), married Hugh of Rouergue 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT ^ Carl Erdmann (1977), The Origin of the Idea of Crusade (Princeton: Princeton University Press), 99-100. 
2 CONT ^ María Eugenia Ibarburu Asurmendi (1999), De capitibus litterarum et aliis figuris: Recull d'estudis miniatura medieval (Barcelona: Edicions Universitat Barcelona, ISBN 8 447 52243 1), 359. The artist has been identified with th
2 CONC e painter of the altar fronts at Sant Sadurní de Rotgers and Aviá. He also illustrated a manuscript of Augustine of Hippo's De civitate Dei (MS. 20 from of the Archivo Capitular de Tortosa). 
