1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wikipédia [http://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paio_Curbo_de_Toronho PT]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Paio Curbo de Toronho''' foi um poderoso fidalgo e cavaleiro medieval do Condado Portucalense com origem em Toronho na Galiza. A Terra do Toronho (Turonium) é um antigo condado ou reguengo situado no Sudoeste da Galiza.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT *https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL.htm#PelayoFernandezCurvoMMariaRodrigMaranon
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         PELAYO Fernández "Curvo" .  "…Pelagius Curvus…" subscribed the charter dated 17 Jul 1137 under which King Alfonso VII donated property confiscated from "Iohannis Lombardi" to Santiago de Compostela[1768].  "…Pelagius Cu
2 CONC rvus…" subscribed the charter dated 30 Sep 1158 under which Fernando II King of León confirmed the archbishop of Santiago de Compostela as capellán and canciller mayor[1769].  "Adefonsus Oseuiz" sold his share in the church of San
2 CONC ta Cristina de Lavadores to "Pelagio Curuo et uxori uestre domne Marie Garcie et filiis et filiabus uestris" by charter dated 20 Apr 1159[1770].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[m''' firstly MARÍA García, daughter of ---.  "Adefonsus Oseuiz" sold his share in the church of Santa Cristina de Lavadores to "Pelagio Curuo et uxori uestre domne Marie Garcie et filiis et filiabus uestris" by charter dated 2
2 CONC 0 Apr 1159[1771].''']'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [secondly] MARÍA Rodríguez de Marañón, daughter of [RODRIGO Pérez de Marañón & his wife ---].  Salazar y Castro records her parentage, marriage and descendants[1772].] 
