2 CONC "Rodríguez" is confirmed by the charter dated 27 May 1182 under which "domina Maria filia comitis Amalrici" donated "casas…in Burgis…in barrio Sancti Romani" to Burgos Cathedral, witnessed by "Petrus Gonsaluez filius Gonsaluo Rois
2 CONC  dus…"[1986], assuming that the son can be identified as the son of Gonzalo de Marañón as appears likely.  Alférez of Alfonso VII King of Castile 7 Feb 1155 to 30 Jul 1157.  "…Gundisaluus de Maranon alferiz imperatoris…" subscribe
2 CONC d the charter dated 7 Feb 1155 under which King Alfonso VII donated property near Lédigos to Santiago de Compostela[1987].  "Aldefonsus…tocius Hyspanie imperator…cum uxore mea imperatrice domna Rica et…filiis meis Sanctio et Ferra
2 CONC ndo regibus" donated property to the abbey of Silos by charter dated 28 Oct 1155, confirmed by "…Gundisalvus de Maranon alferiz imperatoris…"[1988].  "Martinus Fernandez" sold various properties to "Gundisalvo Ferrandiz fratri meo
2 CONC " by charter dated 1156, the dating clause of which names "…Gunzaluo Maranon alfieraz inperatoris…"[1989].  Alfonso VIII King of Castile granted "la villa de Sequilla, sita en el río de Francos…en el término de Cobos de Cerrato" t
