1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gómez Pérez de Toledo Palomeque, Alcalde de los Donceles=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gomez Perez de Toledo y Palomeque was the son of Pedro Fernandez de Toiledo Illan and Urracca Palomeque. He died on 27 January 1291.1
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:  1256 Toledo, New Castile, Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT * Death: 27 Jan 1291 Toledo, New Castile, Spain 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Spouse=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: married 1281 Arabuena Armildez SMAQ, daughter  of Gutierre Armildez b 1231 & m 1258 Mayor Fernandez b 1237 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Child of Gomez Perez de Toledo y Palomeque and Arabuena Armildez==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fernan Gomez de Toledo
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/gomez-perez-palomeque_11224038
2 CONT
2 CONT —
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents are uncertain. Farmerie and Taylor say:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha [de Ayala]’s paternal lineage is clear for four generations before her own.Three  of  them  are  proven  by  a  charter  of  1373,  a  royal  confirmation  of  an exchange of property between Diego Gómez (Sancha’s father), 
2 CONC and Diego’s aunt Constanza, on one part, and a group representing the city of Toledo, on the other, resulting from a renegotiation of a pious testamentary legacy of Diego Gómez’ grandfather Fernán Gómez.10  Here Diego Gómez names 
2 CONC his father as Gómez Pérez, who was son of Fernán Gómez and brother of Constanza. Fernán Gómez’ father appears in all pedigrees as another '''Gómez Pérez''' [emphasis added], also'' alguacil mayor'' of Toledo. About ''his'' father,
2 CONC  however, there is disagreement in the pedigrees.11
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Ricardo Izquierdo Benito, ed., ''Privilegios Reales otorgados a Toledodurante la Edad Media, 1101-1494'' (Toledo, 1990), no. 107, pp. 207-211: a royal confirmation, dated 27 March 1375, of an act dated 15 February 1373.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Salazar y Castro, ''Lara'' 1:348 (and followed by Rubincam), placed Pedro Suarez, ''alguacil  mayor'' of  Toledo  in  1247  and  dead  by 1255  (Angel  González Palencia, ''Los mozarabes de Toledo en los siglos XII y XIII'', 4 
2 CONC vols. (Madrid,1926-30), 1:220) above Gómez Pérez.  This is supported by the repeated use ofthe name ‘Pedro Suarez’ among descendants, and also by the fact that Sancha deAyala’s English descendants quartered ''or, a castle azure'',
2 CONC  which are precisely the arms attributed by Salazar y Castro to this first Pedro Suarez (though onwhat evidence is unknown).  Subsequently in 1716 in his ''Îndice de las Glorias'', p. 588, Salazar y Castro replaced him with Pedro 
2 CONC Fernández, ''alcalde mayor'' of Toledo in 1221, although the same wife was given these two individuals in thetwo  pedigrees. Finally,  Rodríguez  Marquina,  “Linajes  mozárabes  de  Toledo,”pp. 61-64 and chart following, suggests 
2 CONC Pedro Gómez Barroso (also an ancestor of Sancha de Ayala on her mother’s side, AT no. 52) as common ancestor of the Barroso and Gómez de Toledo lineages, though this is supported only by a papal dispensation  for  consanguinity  i
2 CONC n  the  third  degree  between  two  fourteenth-century descendants who probably have other paths of consanguinity.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Todd A. Farmerie and Nathaniel L. Taylor, [https://nltaylor.net/pdfs/a_SanchaNotes.pdf "Notes on the Ancestry of Sancha de Ayala"], prepublication MS of article, subsequently published (with minor emendations) in the ''New Engla
2 CONC nd Historical and Genealogical Register'' 103 (1998), 36-48.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
