1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audeca
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Audeca''' or '''Andeca''' (Latin: Audacer) was the last Suevic King of Galicia from 584 until his deposition in 585. He deposed Eboric and usurped the throne by marrying the young king's mother, Siseguntia (or Sisegutia), the w
2 CONC idow of Eboric's father and predecessor, Miro. He consigned Eboric to a monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT This action gave the Visigothic king Leovigild an excuse to invade the Suevic kingdom, which he did in 585. According to John of Biclar, "Leovigild devastated Galicia, deprived the captured King Audeca of his rule, and brought the
2 CONC  people, treasure, and territory of the Suevi under his own power. He made Galicia a province of the Goths."[1] John goes on to say that he "tonsured [Audeca] and dignified [him] with the honour of the priesthood, after having hel
2 CONC d that of the kingship."[2] The deposed usurper was relegated to the city of Beja. To Isidore of Seville, his deposition meant the end of the Suevic kingdom, which had lasted 177 years from Isidore's starting point of 408: "the ki
2 CONC ngdom which they [the Sueves] held in idle lethargy, they have now lost at an even more shameful cost, although it may seem quite amazing that they had managed to retain up to the present day that which they have now given up with
2 CONC out any show of resistance."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT After Audeca, the Suevic kingdom ceased to exist, but one pretender, Malaric, briefly led opposition to the Visigoths.
2 CONT
2 CONT A coin bearing the inscription ODIACCA REIGES (probably "King Odiacca") has been identified as one belonging to the reign of Audeca. The sole known coin of the type was kept in Madrid and lost in 1936. The only other Suevic king t
2 CONC o mint coins bearing his name that have survived to this day is Rechiar.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriages and descent
2 CONT
2 CONT *Andeca married, firstly, the daughter of King Miro [2].
2 CONT * Then in his second marriage, in 584, he married Siseguta, the widow of Miro [4].
2 CONT
2 CONT No descendants of Andeca are known, neither legitimate nor illegitimate[12].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andeca#Matrimoni_e_discendenza
2 CONT
2 CONT Matrimoni e discendenza
2 CONT
2 CONT # Andeca sposò, in prime nozze, la figlia di re Miro[2].  
2 CONT # Poi in seconde nozze, nel 584, sposò Siseguta, la vedova di Miro[4]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Di Andeca non si conosce alcuna discendenza, né legittima né illegittima[12].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Genealogy
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VANDALS,%20SUEVI,%20VISIGOTHS.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT AUDICA  (-585).  Gregory of Tours records that Audica, a relation of Euric, married the sister of the latter and deposed his brother-in-law, before marrying the widow of his father-in-law[114].  He deposed King Eborico in 584, suc
2 CONC ceeded as AUDICA King of the Suevi.  The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records that "Audeca" succeeded in 584 "in Gallaccia Suevorum regnum" and married "Sisegutiam relictam Mironis regis"[115].  The Visigoths intervened i
2 CONC n support of ex-King Eborico, defeated and deposed King Audica in 585, annexing the Suevi kingdom for themselves[116]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [firstly] --- of the Suevi, daughter of MIRON King of the Suevi.  Gregory of Tours records that Audica, a relation of Euric, married the sister of the latter[117]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [secondly] (584) as her second husband, SISEGUTIA, widow of MIRÓN King of the Suevi, daughter of ---.  The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records that "Audeca" succeeded in 584 "in Gallaccia Suevorum regnum" and married "
2 CONC Sisegutiam relictam Mironis regis"[118]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000194679503972&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Penisola iberica nel 580 circa. In rosso il regno dei Suebi. In verde scuro il regno degli Visigoti. In giallo la provincia bizantina della Spagna. In verde chiaro la zona della penisola iberica sotto il controllo dei Baschi.''
2 CONT
