2 CONC cclesiastically on the archbishopric of Narbonne). He also established relations with the Italian maritime republics of Pisa and Genoa and in 1114 and 1115 raided with them the Moorish pirate strongholds of Majorca and Ibiza. They
2 CONC  became his tributaries and many Christian slaves there were recovered and set free. Ramón Berenguer also raided mainland Muslim dependencies with Pisa's help, such as Valencia, Lleida and Tortosa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toward the end of his life Ramón Berenguer became a Templar. He gave his five Catalonian counties to his eldest son Ramón Berenguer IV and Provence to the younger son Berenguer Ramón.
