1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ermengol VI, Count of Urgell
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Ermengol VI of Urgell)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermengol or Armengol VI (1096 – 1154), called el de Castilla, was the Count of Urgell from 1102 to his death. He was the son and successor of Ermengol V and María Ansúrez.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Valladolid, whence his nickname comes. During his minority, he was under the regency of his grandfather, Pedro Ansúrez, lord of Valladolid, but the real power lay in the hands of Guerau II of Cabrera and Raymond Ber
2 CONC engar III of Barcelona. With their help, the young count count conquered Balaguer in 1106 and made it his capital.
2 CONT
2 CONT Armengol collaborated with Alfonso the Battler in the 1118 capture of Zaragoza and in the expedition of Alfonso VII the Emperor against Almería in 1147. He had good relations with the House of Barcelona and he accompanied Raymond 
2 CONC Berengar IV's to Provence in 1144. In 1149, he assisted Raymond Berengar in the conquest and repopulation of Lleida, which was thenceforward a city of his dominion. Ermengol died in Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1129, Ermengol married Arsenda de Cabrera, daughter of the viscount Ponç of Àger. Besides his successor, Ermengol VII, he had two daughters with her: Sibylla, who married Ramon Folch, viscount of Cardona, and Stephanie, who mar
2 CONC ried Arnau Mir of Pallars Jussà.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1135, Ermengol married a second time to Elvira, daughter of Rodrigo of Lara and Sancha of Castile. To this union were born Galceran de Sales and Mary, lady of Almenara.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Armengol''', VI  Conde de Urgel
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
