1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sancha González
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 1131
2 CONT
2 CONT      Sancha González was born circa 1131. She married Fernando Pérez de Traba, son of conde de Traba Pedro Fróilaz de Traba, before 1154.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernando Pérez de Traba b. circa 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Teresa Fernández de Traba b. c 1154, d. 7 Feb 1180
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Marriage and offspring
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fernando_Pérez_de_Traba
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernando Pérez de Traba (c. 1100-Santiago de Compostela, November 1, 1155)[1], was a nobleman of Galicia, count and lieutenant in Traba and Trastámara, he resided for a time in the Portucalense County. He was the son of Pedro Froi
2 CONC laz Count of Traba, of the then most powerful strain of the Kingdom of Galicia, the House of Traba, and Countess Urraca Froilaz.[ 2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Countess ''Sancha González'', daughter of Count Gonzalo Ansúrez and Urraca Bermúdez,[a] with whom he had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # María Fernández de Traba (d. 1168), wife of Count Ponce Giraldo de Cabrera,[8].
2 CONT # Gonzalo Fernández de Traba (d. 1160), count, married to Countess Berenguela Rodríguez, daughter of Count Rodrigo Vélaz and Countess Urraca Álvarez.[ 8] He was lieutenant in Montenegro and Sarria in 1178.[ 9]
2 CONT # Urraca Fernández de Traba (d. 1199), married to Juan Arias from whom she had offspring. Both were the ayos of Infante Alfonso, later Alfonso IX of León.[ 10][11] Urraca was already a widow in 1191 when she visited Oviedo and mad
2 CONC e donations to the monastery of San Pelayo. Tested in 1199.[ 12]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT Professor Margarita Torres (p. 112) says that Sancha was the daughter of Count Gonzalo Peláez. However, according to Antonio Sánchez de Mora in his thesis on the House of Lara (Volume I, p. 70), Sancha was the daughter of Count Go
2 CONC nzalo Ansúrez and Countess Urraca Bermúdez. On April 24, 1142, Sancha made a donation to the monastery of Lorenzana in which he mentions his grandfather Bermudo Ovéquiz, confirming the genealogy proposed by Sánchez de Mora.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fernando_Pérez_de_Traba
