0 @N6000000002187750864@ NOTE Sancha of León
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancha of León (1013 in Leon, Spain-1067 in Leon, Spain) was a daughter of Alfonso V of Leon by Elvira Mendes and Queen consort of Castile. She married Ferdinand I of León in 1032. She was a devout Catholic.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT She had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancho II of Castile (1040s - 1067). First son. 
1 CONT Alfonso VI of Castile (1040s - July 1, 1109). Second son. 
1 CONT García II of Galicia and Portugal (1040s - 1090s). Third son. 
1 CONT Elvira of Toro. Ruler of the city Toro. 
1 CONT Urraca of Zamora, Infanta of Castile. 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible, Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families Vol. 3 (chart 2186) by Michel L. Call ISBN 1-933194-22-7 
